- entry .JavaLongInstant   a bare `Long` as an instant, counting milliseconds since the epoch
-     An object which is `Long is Abstractable across Instants to Long` and `Long is
-     Instantiable across Instants from Long`, both the identity, offered as the given
-     `instantInterfaces.javaLongInstant`, imported by name. It is what lets an instant be
-     taken or given as the raw `System.currentTimeMillis` form. Note the asymmetry with
-     `JavaLongDuration`, whose `Long` counts nanoseconds. Its members `apply` and `genericize`
-     both return their argument unchanged.
+ entry .JavaLongInstant   um `Long` puro como instante, contando milissegundos desde a época
+     Um objeto que é `Long is Abstractable across Instants to Long` e `Long is Instantiable
+     across Instants from Long`, ambos a identidade, oferecido como o given
+     `instantInterfaces.javaLongInstant`, importado pelo nome. É o que permite que um instante
+     seja recebido ou dado na forma bruta de `System.currentTimeMillis`. Observe a assimetria com
+     `JavaLongDuration`, cujo `Long` conta nanossegundos. Seus membros `apply` e `genericize`
+     devolvem ambos seu argumento inalterado.

=     both return their argument unchanged.
